              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "چکانا — chukānā — \"to pay off, to settle (a bill)\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "چکانا (chukānā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from cukk, \"fall short of, stop\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 4848). It is the causing form of chuknā, \"to be finished\". CDIAL takes cukk from Prakrit cukka, \"fallen, mistaken\", which replaced Sanskrit cyuta, \"fallen\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
